只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh-switchman who is a plugin for deepseek harness","id":"gh:1394606163","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-switchman","slug":"mrzturn/dsh-switchman","topics":["context-management","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","orchestration"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh-switchman who is a plugin for deepseek harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-switchman"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文 | 繁體中文 | 日本語 | 한국어 | Español | Français | Deutsch | Italiano | Português | Русски"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"*English** | 简体中文 | 繁體中文 | 日本語 | 한국어 | Español | Français | Deutsch | Italiano | Português | Русский"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **The switchman family**, same author, same dispatch doctrine: opencode-switchman (the OpenCode or"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"iginal) · zcode-switchman (the ZCode port) · **dsh-switchman** (this repo, the DeepSeek Harness edit"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"l) · zcode-switchman (the ZCode port) · **dsh-switchman** (this repo, the DeepSeek Harness edition)."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> A water meter on the context; every task finds its own lane."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why you need it"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Two pains creep in once you've worked in DSH for a while. First, sessions get heavier the longer the"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"y run: history bloats the context into hundreds of thousands of tokens, the model starts forgetting,"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" slowing down, costing more — and a manual /compact loses detail. Second, the main model does everyt"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"hing itself: chasing files, running tests, reconciling data — most of that work belongs on a cheaper"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"self: chasing files, running tests, reconciling data — most of that work belongs on a cheaper model."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"dsh-switchman is a plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Once installed, the main model stops doing and"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" starts dispatching: measure the watermark, pick a lane, hand out tasks, check acceptance. It's not "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"a new model — it's a dispatch doctrine hooked onto DSH plus a settings page, and it does eight thing"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"new model — it's a dispatch doctrine hooked onto DSH plus a settings page, and it does eight things:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**1. Context watermark: long sessions don't blow up.** Every turn counts session tokens in real time"},{"id":"p9s2","text":", and three escalating lines tighten the screws: 80k (soft, adjustable) nudges \"time to delegate\"; 9"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"5k (hard) shrinks the single-read budget and steers toward wrap-up; 150k (force) hands over automati"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"cally — writes the handover document (the append-only session log is the full-fidelity backup), comp"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"acts the context, wakes the session to continue, task unbroken. Background subagents still running a"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"t handover aren't lost either: their ids, tasks, and report paths go into the handover document, so "},{"id":"p9s7","text":"the resumed session knows where to collect reports and never dispatches twice. Every subagent carrie"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"s its own hard cap and exits after writing its HANDOFF summary. When the automatic intervention does"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"n't suit you, take over manually: `/ctx-pause` stops all watermark actions (measurement keeps runnin"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"g, the live watermark line switches to paused — it just stops acting), `/ctx-resume` restores them a"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"t any time — after a DSH restart the enforcement also comes back on its own, a temporary let-go, not"},{"id":"p9s12","text":" a permanent off; `/ctx-handover` doesn't wait for the watermark to hit the ceiling and starts the s"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"anent off; `/ctx-handover` doesn't wait for the watermark to hit the ceiling and starts the s [长行截断]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Bundled skills"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- **db-query** — read-only MySQL / Redis verification: run SQL to reconcile data, inspect cache keys"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" / TTL, cross-database consistency checks; every write refused. Needs one-time initialization before"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" first use (see below).\n- **git-commit-message** — generates disciplined commit messages; text only,"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" never runs git for you.\n- **requirement-docs** — the house standard for requirement analysis / PRD "},{"id":"p12s5","text":"/ design docs; output is archived to `docs/requirements-and-design/`."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"1. **Install** — have an agent run it in any session, or use the Web plugin management page:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Or install from a local checkout (link mode; after an update, `remove_bundle` + `install_bundle` aga"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"nstall from a local checkout (link mode; after an update, `remove_bundle` + `install_bundle` again):"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Or with the `dsh` CLI in a terminal — pick the profile matching how you run it:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"2. **Restart DSH** — quit the app completely and reopen it (a page refresh doesn't count); only then"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" does the client module table recognize the bundle."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"3. **Configure** — Settings → dsh-switchman, or \"Switchman Dispatch Center\" in the home sidebar. It'"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"s a single page of config and looks like this — walk it top to bottom and you're done:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- **Interface** — the plugin's own UI language. The dropdown in the shot sits at English — a live pr"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"eview of switching; the shipped default is Auto (follows the DSH app language). Picking a language f"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"lips the whole page on the spot and is remembered after save; switch back to Auto anytime.\n- **Langu"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"ages** — the languages of agent output. The scope in the shot is \"Global (this profile)\" (per-projec"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"t works too, each reading `.switchman/lang.json`); the reply / code comments / documents dropdowns i"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"n the shot all sit at English, each displayed as \"endonym (tag)\" — e.g. \"English (en)\" — with a \"cur"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"rent: …\" status line beneath each. Leaving all three unset is fine too: asked once on first use, rem"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"embered from then on.\n- **Dispatch pools** — six cards in two rows of three: economy, mechanical, ma"},{"id":"p22s9","text":"in on top; hard, vision, review below. Tick candidate models grouped by provider; tick \"manual order"},{"id":"p22s10","text":"\" and a card becomes a numbered priority list reorderable with ↑ ↓ ×; every route can pin a thinking"},{"id":"p22s11","text":" effort (default \"follow lane\"). The summary line at the top updates live — in the shot: \"4/6 pools "},{"id":"p22s12","text":"configured · 2 ranked · mode advice\".\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- The host half (`index.js` + `host/`) injects the byte-stable system-prompt sections (language / la"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"nes / watermark protocol / teams) plus the live watermark line through the tail runtime-context snap"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"shot (a channel that appends instead of rewriting the prompt head, so the provider prompt cache stay"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"s intact), the read-budget plus enforce double gate, and four slash commands (the ctx trio + `/visio"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"n`). A saved setting takes effect at the very next prompt assembly — no restart.\n- The client half ("},{"id":"p24s6","text":"`client.js`) renders the settings page, the ⚡ badge and ◇ model marker in the session header, and th"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"e live handover indicator; config snapshots are read and written through the Host route family.\n- Th"},{"id":"p24s8","text":"e \"Switchman Dispatch Center\" entry in the home sidebar opens that same settings page as a center pa"},{"id":"p24s9","text":"nel in one click; the original settings entry stays.\n- `cordis.patch.yml` keeps the factory preset p"},{"id":"p24s10","text":"lugin list fully intact and only extends the persona suffix; the Agent Teams tools themselves come f"},{"id":"p24s11","text":"rom the factory bundle and switch on automatically with teams mode."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
